<header><p class="st-kicker">protectorate · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Cretan State</h1><p class="st-meta">1898 CE – 1913 CE · capital Chania</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Autonomous Crete under great-power protection from 1898, a stepping stone to union with Greece and the launch pad of Eleftherios Venizelos.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a> rose repeatedly against Ottoman rule in the 19th century. After the revolt of 1897 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greco-turkish-war-1897">Greco-Turkish War</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> occupied the island and forced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> to accept its autonomy under nominal suzerainty. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-george-of-greece-and-denmark">Prince George of Greece</a> became High Commissioner in December 1898, with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kydonia">Chania</a> as capital.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Cretan State had its own constitution, assembly, gendarmerie, currency and stamps, though foreign troops remained. Prince George's autocratic style clashed with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eleftherios-venizelos">Eleftherios Venizelos</a>, who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theriso-revolt">Therisos revolt</a> in 1905. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandros-zaimis">Alexandros Zaimis</a> replaced the prince in 1906. Most of the population was Greek <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a>, with a significant Muslim minority.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1908 the Cretan assembly declared union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkan-wars">Balkan Wars</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> renounced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a>, and it was formally united with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-greece">Kingdom of Greece</a> in December 1913. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eleftherios-venizelos">Venizelos</a> had by then become prime minister of Greece.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/cretan-state.jpg" alt="Cretan State" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Vectorization: Froztbyte · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Cretan_State.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1898 CE – 1913 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>protectorate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Chania</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Prince George of Greece, Alexandros Zaimis, Eleftherios Venizelos</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity, Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Autonomous Crete, Kritiki Politeia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1906&amp;focus=cretan-state" aria-label="Cretan State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5287 894 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Cretan State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5607 1150L5709 970M5607 1150L4997 651M5607 1150L6487 457M5607 1150L5591 1068"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5709 970h0M4997 651h0M6487 457h0M5591 1068h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5607 1150h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5607 1150h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Chania. <a href="/atlas?year=1906&amp;focus=cretan-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
